      "document": {
        "resourceId": "IP1-general-document-03",
        "sourceVersionId": "IP1-general-document-03-A",
        "title": "Measuring a file-processing batch",
        "format": "html",
        "extractorVersion": "structured-v2-compatible-fixture",
        "structureProvenance": "assistant-authored; not an extraction run",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "IP1-G05-B01",
            "order": 0,
            "kind": "heading",
            "text": "Measuring a file-processing batch",
            "metadata": {
              "schemaVersion": 1,
              "links": [],
              "level": 2
            },
            "textSha256": "5eed1d0ea691a2149135dbf87a9755a2c3c09d18867e8b6b61bba78bdbba3c09"
          },
          {
            "id": "IP1-G05-B02",
            "order": 1,
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "The lab records the number of completed files and the processing time in minutes. Its active timer begins after setup. Loading the software before that timer starts is setup overhead.",
            "metadata": {
              "schemaVersion": 1,
              "links": []
            },
            "textSha256": "88f9d3dcc17b4e858ec76e2daaa5a758a0facb196b28f1c626be953a599dff4b"
          },
          {
            "id": "IP1-G05-B03",
            "order": 2,
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "Divide the number of completed files by the processing time to obtain the measure in files per minute. This quotient uses only the interval recorded by the active timer. It excludes the setup overhead described above, even if setup takes longer than processing. The log records interrupted runs separately; do not combine an interrupted run with a completed batch when calculating this measure.",
            "metadata": {
              "schemaVersion": 1,
              "links": []
            },
            "textSha256": "d32a5a20a1232ac399fcef81c419107f332ff697b965b8dfbed36d28f7daaa90"
          },
          {
            "id": "IP1-G05-B04",
            "order": 3,
            "kind": "paragraph",
            "text": "The operator stores the raw counts and timer readings so another person can reproduce the reported measure.",
            "metadata": {
              "schemaVersion": 1,
              "links": []
            },
            "textSha256": "6b260274352851faf120630e18b84fa3bee409c98b088f885d10ea4747237042"
          }
        ],
        "titleKo": ""
      },
      "targetBlockId": "IP1-G05-B03"
    },
